{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Code Quality Review",
  "description": "Analyzes modified source code files for potential improvements including code smells, design patterns, and best practices. Generates suggestions for improving readability, maintainability, and performance while maintaining existing functionality.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "*.py",
      "*.jsx",
      "*.js",
      "*.ts",
      "*.tsx"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Analyze the modified code for potential improvements. Focus on:\n1. Code smells (long methods, duplicated logic, magic numbers, deep nesting)\n2. Design patterns that could simplify the code\n3. Best practices for the language/framework being used\n4. Readability improvements (naming, structure, comments)\n5. Maintainability concerns (tight coupling, missing error handling)\n6. Performance optimizations (unnecessary re-renders, inefficient queries, redundant operations)\n\nProvide concise, actionable suggestions that maintain existing functionality. Prioritize the most impactful improvements. Use Brazilian Portuguese for any UI-related suggestions to match the project conventions."
  }
}